{
  "dom_id": "step-q58208",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Solve for $y$ where $16=3y+1.$",
  "worked_solution": "To save time, we will keep the variable on the right-hand side as we solve. First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $1$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =3y+1 \\\\ 16-1 & =3y+1-1 \\\\ 15 & =3y+0 \\\\ 15 & =3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 & =3y \\\\ \\frac{15}{3} & =\\frac{3y}{3} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}y}{\\cancel{3}} \\\\ 5 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $5=y,$ we conclude that the solution is $y=5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
